WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.886
The final coding exercise combines preservation
cardinality and aggregation The

00:00:06.899 --> 00:00:11.755
result must contain one row per department including
departments with zero activity

00:00:13.503 --> 00:00:18.795
Start from departments because that is the
population to preserve LEFT JOIN

00:00:18.821 --> 00:00:24.745
admissions by department and LEFT JOIN medical staff
by department Because

00:00:24.771 --> 00:00:28.784
a department may have several admissions and several
staff members the combined

00:00:28.811 --> 00:00:34.326
detail rows can multiply Use distinct identifiers
when counting admissions and

00:00:34.353 --> 00:00:39.872
staff Group by department so the final grain is one
department

00:00:39.898 --> 00:00:45.075
per row After Run and Check look for the department
with no

00:00:45.088 --> 00:00:50.683
activity It should still appear with zero counts
Then inspect a busy

00:00:50.709 --> 00:00:54.775
department and make sure its counts represent
original admissions and staff members

00:00:54.999 --> 00:01:00.910
not joined combinations This is a realistic example
of why join logic

00:01:00.936 --> 00:01:03.515
and aggregation logic must be designed together
